  "text": {
    "intro": "The Thistledown Ascent is less a race than a slow argument conducted at two thousand feet.\nFive pilots are involved. Determine each pilot's start time, landing site and ballast.\n- **Pilot**: Grover, Delphine, Horatio, Anneliese and Montague.\n- **Start time** (listed from earlier to later): 8am, 9am, 10am, 11am and noon.\n- **Landed at**: a cabbage field, a flooded quarry, a golf course bunker, a caravan park and a cricket pitch.\n- **Ballast**: iron filings, bottled water, dried beans, rock salt and lead shot.\nEvery pilot has a different start time, landing site and ballast, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The pilot who comes down in a golf course bunker launches at 9am.",
      "The pilot who comes down in a caravan park is earlier than 10am in start time order.",
      "The pilot who carries rock salt and 11am are exactly one hour apart in start time order, in one direction or the other.",
      "Montague does not launch at 8am.",
      "The pilot who carries iron filings does not launch at noon.",
      "Delphine falls somewhere between the pilot who carries bottled water and the pilot who carries rock salt in start time order.",
      "The pilot who comes down in a flooded quarry is exactly one hour earlier than Horatio, with no start time in between.",
      "The pilot who carries lead shot and the pilot who comes down in a flooded quarry are exactly two hours apart in start time order.",
      "The pilot who carries rock salt is exactly one hour earlier than Grover, with no start time in between.",
      "The pilot who comes down in a cabbage field falls somewhere between the pilot who carries iron filings and the pilot who carries lead shot in start time order."
